From e4e1e7ef3f1f8126d7d6c90167376f2ac855a5c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HighAsCG Assembly <assembly@highascg.local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:21:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] =?UTF-8?q?fix(oal):=20initialize=20the=20SwrContext?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20pointer=20before=20swr=5Falloc=5Fset=5Fopts2=20=E2=80=94=20u?=
 =?UTF-8?q?pstream=2085fa10952?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

swr_alloc_set_opts2 treats a non-null *ps as an existing context to reuse. The Enhanced OAL
consumer passed an uninitialized pointer, so whether initialize() crashed depended on stack
garbage. Reproduced on the HighAsCG box: AMCP "ADD 2 SYSTEM-AUDIO DEVICE_NAME ..." segfaulted in
av_opt_set_chlayout <- swr_alloc_set_opts2 <- oal_consumer::initialize. Same one-line fix as
CasparCG/server 85fa10952 (#1714), which 2.5.1 ships but the Enhanced consumer never got.
HighAsCG WO-847.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MxpJi7QVXYQA38FT76gLNj
---
 src/modules/oal/consumer/oal_consumer.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/modules/oal/consumer/oal_consumer.cpp b/src/modules/oal/consumer/oal_consumer.cpp
index dfa94f824..c6b62764f 100644
--- a/src/modules/oal/consumer/oal_consumer.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/oal/consumer/oal_consumer.cpp
@@ -206,7 +206,7 @@ struct oal_consumer : public core::frame_consumer
             av_channel_layout_default(&from, format_desc_.audio_channels);
             av_channel_layout_default(&to, 2); // stereo
 
-            SwrContext* raw;
+            SwrContext* raw = nullptr; // swr_alloc_set_opts2 reuses a non-null *ps (upstream 85fa10952)
             swr_alloc_set_opts2(&raw,
                 &to,   AV_SAMPLE_FMT_S16, format_desc_.audio_sample_rate,
                 &from, AV_SAMPLE_FMT_S32, format_desc_.audio_sample_rate,
