The Enhanced screen consumer (the source of #1718) fell back to a fixed 16:9 when a consumer had
neither <aspect-ratio> nor <width>/<height>: AMCP "ADD n SCREEN" on a 1600x400 channel opened a
711x400 window and squeezed the picture (stock and #1718's last revision derive it from the
format's square dimensions). Ported from the PR head:
- aspect_ratio 0.0 = auto; parse_aspect_ratio returns auto for empty/default/invalid input and
  accepts "W/H" next to "W:H" and decimals;
- effective_aspect_ratio() feeds uniform/none/uniform_to_fill and the windowed resize lock;
- a0c5f9c99f: the initial glViewport is the window size, not the channel format.
Kept from the fork: force-linear-filter, the visibility toggle, the verbose logs, and no
brightness/saturation (dropped upstream after review). Configs that set <width>/<height> (every
HighAsCG-generated screen) are unaffected: their aspect is still width/height.

Verified on Xvfb: 1600x400 channel, AMCP ADD and a bare <screen/> open 1600x400 (were 711x400);
<aspect-ratio>3840/1080</aspect-ratio> opens 1422x400 (was 711x400, "/" unparsed). HighAsCG WO-847.

