From e8d457ec6321f2556b999decde033b3cf7a7de71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HighAsCG Assembly <assembly@highascg.local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:24:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] =?UTF-8?q?oal:=20one=20device=20+=20context=20per=20o?=
 =?UTF-8?q?utput=20device,=20selected=20per=20thread=20(ALC=5FEXT=5Fthread?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=5Flocal=5Fcontext)=20=E2=80=94=20the=20#1714=20device=20half?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20for=20the=20Enhanced=20consumer?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each Enhanced OAL consumer opened its own device and made its context current process-wide
(alcMakeContextCurrent). With two <system-audio> consumers the last one's context received every
AL call of both, so neither source gated its channel: on the HighAsCG box two 1080p50 channels
with system-audio on HDMI 1 / HDMI 2 ran their clips at 2.1x-3.7x real time and teardown hung. A
second consumer on an already open device failed with "Failed to initialize audio device" (the
"pre-existing" ADD AUDIO error in HighAsCG WO-613).

Now, as upstream #1714 / 2.5.1 does it:
- device::open() resolves the configured name exactly as before (space-insensitive match, unknown
  -> default) and returns a shared device per resolved name (weak_ptr registry under a mutex);
  consumers on the same device each get their own source on the shared context;
- every AL entry point (initialize/teardown on the executor, each frame on the channel output
  thread) selects the context with alcSetThreadContext and releases it afterwards; without the
  extension it falls back to the old process-wide context with a warning.
The Enhanced send() flow (deferred future gating the channel on AL_BUFFERS_PROCESSED) is
unchanged; the OAL choice of WO-613 (Enhanced over #1714) stands.

Verified on the box with a scratch instance (AMCP 5262): two devices 1.00x / 1.00x (old 2.06x /
2.10x and 3.70x / 3.70x), same device shared 1.00x / 1.00x (old: second consumer failed), AMCP
ADD (shared) / REMOVE 2-500 / ADD on another device with the clip at 1.00x throughout, clean exit.
HighAsCG WO-847.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MxpJi7QVXYQA38FT76gLNj
